Z||000023||DaRkLoRD||08-03-2000||04:16 AM||||whee.. there's a LOT of cars I hate... where to begin...<P>early 80s station wagons.. <BR>el caminos.. <BR>just about any non-muscle car from the 50s, 60s or 70s... <BR>family cars of the early-mid 80s (ugly  boxes!!!!!) <BR>ford festivas and other cars with a similar appearance.. (I hate the sound they make too... like a freaking WIND UP TOY)<BR>did I mention el caminos? <BR>old toyota minivans, <BR>yugos etc, <BR>pintos, <BR>the cr@p they replaced the dodge charger with.. <BR>ford aerostars (we used to have one, they're piles of s**t) <BR>big old rusty pickup trucks.. <BR>any car that has mismatched body panels that the owner didn't bother to spend $5 on a can of spraypaint for.. <BR>ford tempos.. <BR>1970s camaros (I'm gonna get flamed for that one.. lol) <BR>the batmobile from the 1960s tv show.. (best thing about the show was Batgirl.. mmm.... batgirl... hehehehe) <BR>PT cruisers, <BR>old vw beetles (new ones are better, but still slightly weird looking..)<BR>crappy honda accords etc. that are riced up..<BR>any vehicle that is all rusted out and hasn't been repaired or scrapped.. <BR>any car that's more than 5% chrome.. <BR>any car with <B>TAIL FINS</B>.....<BR>el caminos..........<BR>early 80s Jeep Cherokees (I love the new ones though..)<BR>the car Mr. Bean drives.. (austin mini?)<BR>old dodge caravans, with peeling, faded wood veneer on the sides.. and 5" fog lights attached to the front bumper (there's one of those in my town.. haha)<BR>any car with repairs made with DUCT TAPE....<BR>1980s pontiac grand am<BR>pontiac 6000 LE<BR>el camino...... (yes, I REALLY hate those things.........)<BR>cars with the front lowered so much the airdam is scraping the road and the rear jacked up so much it could back over a tree stump and not notice......<BR>1980s ford taurus.. <BR>any year ford taurus wagon..<P>I could go on for a LONG time.. but I gotta get up in 4 hours, so I should stop now and get some sleep.. but one last car...<P>a neglected 84 Fiero base coupe.. with a broken luggage rack, 13" wheels and cheap hubcaps that don't match!! (I saw this car today..) paint was so faded it looked orange.. interior was ripped up.. the radio had been removed, there were cut wires just sticking out of the hole in the dash.. battery was held in place by bungee cords.. the rear fascia had bumper stickers plastered all over it to cover up damage... front airdam was gone.. (ripped right off.. looked like it'd hit a curb or something) anyway, it was sad seeing a fiero like that.. and I never realized how much the ground effects, aero fascias and a wing improve the looks of a notchback Fiero.....<P>oh yeah.. almost forgot...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR><B>EL CAMINOS!!!!!!!!!!!</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
