Z||000045||StuGood||08-03-2000||08:57 PM||||For consistently ugly vehicles, in my book, Citroen has them all beat.  Most of the ones I'm familiar with look like hard-shelled beetles (not VW's) crawling along the street.  You kind of want to step on them, and put them out of their misery.  Sorry if I offended anyone - but it's only my opinion, and you asked  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>Of course, there are plenty of "ugly American" examples, too.  Remember the "aero-style" GM sedans?  Were those an attempt to make full-size cars look like big Chevy Citations, or what?  <P>For what it's worth, among US cars, AMC made some of the ugliest ones, at least in my eyes.  Pacer and Matador are prime examples.  Forgot all about the Matador until reading the earlier post.  They look like someone really <B>worked</B> at making those ugly, IMHO.  <P>But, AMC just wasn't consistent enough to deserve the all-time ugly award - I kind of <B>liked</B> the Javelins.  Did I ever own one? No.  Would I want one now? Nope.       ||||reg||12
