Z||000050||deceler8||08-04-2000||04:19 PM||||In the mid '70's, the Matador actually had some style...it wasn't a box at least...<P>I saw one the other day that was in mint condition and I thought the styling still looked unique (I didn't say I thought it was beautiful...)<P>As to ugly, 1961 Dodge Lancer/Plymouth Valiant takes the cake. And the 1965-66 Dodge Monaco/Polara is neck and neck. Square, oddly proportioned, and granny-looking. I think Jack Lemmon drove a 66 Polara in "Grumpy Old Men".<P>Ugliest Fiero I've ever seen is an '85 coupe about two blocks from me...13" wheels with white letter tires (all four flat), Holley side scoop, silver paint burned off hood, roof, and decklid, trashed interior...I'd buy it for $100 just to get it off the road (it's killin' my resale value and that of every other Fiero in town)...||||reg||1
Z||000051||frontal lobe||08-04-2000||06:22 PM||||Regarding the Aztec, you wouldn't think someone with vision bad enough to buy one would still be able to qualify for a driver's license.||||reg||1
Z||000052||stimpy||08-04-2000||08:09 PM||||Reliant Scimitar! Talk about a freak-mobile, it's a three wheeler that is prone to tipping at speeds faster then walking.<P>The Toyta Corolla SR5 4wd wagon from 84, looked like an ATM on wheels.<P>Dodge Omni. Enough said.<P>Any of the 80's X-cars with extra ugly credit for the Pontiac Pheonix 4 door hatchback.<P>The Oldsmobile Cutlass Salon.<P>The 2nd generation Cadilac Seville.<P>The Ford Escort EXP!!! <P>And that Toyota Echo is withou question the most hideous aotomotive atrocity in the small car market, only outdone by that acid trip Aztek!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
